# 2. CW-002 — Dobrushin / filtering / decision horizons

## Dobrushin contraction theory
Role:
- total-variation contraction and submultiplicativity.
CWR theorem built from it:
\[
r(E_t)\le(1-1/n)\eta(T_{0:t})
\]
for the entire future observation tail, with reset-kernel sharpness.
Ownership:
Dobrushin contraction is classical; the Le Cam future-tail decision formulation remains a synthesis under collision audit.

## Birkhoff (projective contraction)
Role:
- Hilbert metric contraction for positive operators.
Key formula used:
\[
\tau(A)=\tanh(\Delta(A)/4).
\]
CWR use:
history-uniform filter forgetting because diagonal likelihood scaling and normalization are projectively harmless.

## Atar–Zeitouni (1997)
Role:
- direct prior art for nonlinear-filter exponential stability / memory length using Birkhoff contraction.
Ownership correction:
“Hilbert metric gives pathwise filter forgetting” is classical.

## Budhiraja–Ocone
Role:
- Hilbert/Birkhoff machinery in discrete-time filter stability.
Ownership:
classical filter-stability engine.

## McDonald–Yüksel (2019/2020)
Role:
- Dobrushin-style filter stability combining transition and observation coefficients;
- controlled extensions.
Ownership:
expectation-level TV filter-contraction machinery is classical.

