# 6. Linear recurrences / orbit problems / Markov-chain arithmetic

## Vahanwala (2024), Skolem/Positivity completeness of ergodic Markov chains
Role:
- direct collision with the lab’s “contractive shell embeds signed recurrence” mechanism.
Published construction:
\[
M=S+D,\qquad SD=DS=0,\qquad M^n=S+D^n,
\]
with a disturbance entry proportional to an LRS term times an exponential scaling.
CWR correction:
generic contractive-shell LRS embedding is prior art.
CWR exact deduction:
with uniform stationary \(S=J\), the construction is in fact doubly stochastic because \(D\) has zero row and column sums.

## Kannan–Lipton Orbit Problem
Role:
- point orbit reachability for a single rational linear operator is polynomial-time decidable.
CWR structural contrast:
point targets can be easier than halfspace sign targets.

## Ouaknine–Worrell — LRS Positivity / Ultimate Positivity
Claims used:
- general Positivity decidable through low order (order \(\le5\));
- order 6 touches deep Diophantine approximation obstacles;
- simple-root Positivity decidable through higher order;
- simple Ultimate Positivity decidable more generally.
CWR use:
general nonreversible bistochastic stationary-cutpoint state-count frontier.

## De les Coves–Graf–Klingler–Netzer (2025)
Major correction:
Positivity is decidable for LRS whose characteristic roots are all real, in arbitrary order.
CWR consequence:
for a *single reversible rational Markov chain*, strict halfspace crossing is decidable in arbitrary dimension.

## Akshay et al. (STACS 2020 line)
Role:
